Z||000014||2xsess||12-03-2000||01:44 AM||||I agree, PBS you have been a great ambassador for your group  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Wow, I feel like I've had the priveledge of owning a few awesome cars now   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>90 Celica GTS with all the toys and a 5spd<P>92 Prelude Si only thing it didn't have was CD and it also was a 5spd.<P>and of course 5 Fieros covering almost all production years, dang, somehow I missed 87     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>The Celica handled great on PA back country roads, I can't remember the tire size but I paid $200 each for Bridgestone potenzas on it, it really sucked in the snow though. The prelude handled good, even better after it got the 2" dropped springs on it. All the Fieros handled great, the only one I ever really thought was lacking was my 86GT but, I think that car had been seriously wrecked at one point in it's life.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||10
